From 4451218f660ede201bb0aec8e03f15daabddd51b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment <experiment@invalid>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:39:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: collapse the experiment build arms into the
 station driver

The driver grew as a chain of seventeen default-off Kconfig arms plus two
module parameters that selected among lifetimes, windows and observers.
Only one combination is contract-correct and has passed the 120 s and 600 s
gates: the checked stable-epoch receive path with the initial GTK, the
connected lifetime, PID reuse, depth-four TX and the progress-aware yield.
Make that combination the only build arm.

Keep the compile-time symbols the source still uses, but turn them into
def_bool facts that follow MT6797_MAC80211 instead of user choices, and
retire the four arms the working driver never takes: the read-only scan
tuning samples, the 50-second idle-tail comparison, the register-write
mask-control comparison (the only write through the diagnostic path, which
the firmware contract forbids), and the dormant lifetime-prerequisite
helpers that had no caller. The native-delivery diagnostic is now never
armed and the stable epoch is always armed; both former module parameters
become constants so the compiler drops the dead branches. No command,
descriptor, deadline, credit or data-path behaviour changes for the arm
that runs on the device.

Internal experiment archive; synthetic non-certifying author,
not submission-ready.
